@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title SVM — Selection Map (margin, kernel, slack)
' Synthesis of the support-vector family: when a margin classifier beats a tree or a net
' Level:  1

actor "Human expert\nn samples, d features" as H

component "Linear SVM\nw·x + b = 0" as LIN <<app>>
component "Kernel SVM\nRBF / polynomial" as KER <<host>>
component "Soft margin\nslack + penalty C" as SOFT <<async>>
database  "Support vectors\nthe only points that matter" as SV <<db>>

H ARROW_MAIN LIN : linearly separable,\nd large vs n
H ARROW_OPTIONAL KER : non-linear boundary,\nn small enough for the Gram matrix
H ARROW_MAIN SOFT : real data — overlap\nand label noise
LIN ARROW_MAIN SV : solution is defined by\nactive constraints only
KER ARROW_MAIN SV
SOFT ARROW_MAIN SV

note bottom of SV
  **Reach for an SVM when** d is large relative to n,
  the decision boundary matters more than a
  probability, and the dataset fits in memory.
  **Reach elsewhere when** n is large (kernel cost is
  superlinear), features are heterogeneous and
  tabular (""../trees-and-ensembles/""), or you need
  representation learning (""../neural-networks/"").
end note
@enduml
